=== WHAT WAS BUILT (parity with the web source, read end-to-end) ===
  SecuritySection is the Security section of the Vehicle Detail page: a GlassPanel with a
  Shield-icon "Security" header over either a four-tile MetricCard grid (when a security
  reading is present) or an EmptyState ("No security data available"). The web component is
  a pure presentational leaf fed TWO props — securityData (a SecurityEvent) and state (a
  VehicleState) — by the Vehicle Detail page. The native surface reproduces its data,
  composition, every state, and i18n keys via shared P1/S8 state-holder seams (no view I/O).

  Composition (web → native), all FOUR MetricCards reproduced VERBATIM (not stubbed):
   1. Locked  — state.is_locked ? "Yes" : "No"; lock.fill when locked else lock.open.fill;
                green accent when locked else cyan (the web Lock/Unlock + green/cyan flip).
   2. Sentry  — state.sentry_mode ? "Active" : "Off"; eye.fill glyph; green when active else
                cyan (web Eye + green/cyan).
   3. Doors   — door_state shown verbatim when present + non-empty (web
                `door_state != null && door_state !== '' ? String(door_state) : null`,
                reproduced incl. the JS String() coercion), else localized "Closed";
                door.left.hand.closed glyph; cyan when a door state is present else green.
   4. Windows — `{{count}} open` when windowOpenCount > 0 else "Closed"; car.fill glyph;
                cyan when open else green. windowOpenCount ports the web inline helper
                EXACTLY: over fd/fp/rd/rp_window, coerce `typeof v==='number' ? v : Number(v)`
                and count finite readings strictly > 0 (a nil field is skipped; a NaN
                coercion is not finite so not counted).

  JS coercion fidelity (the heart of the web component): SecuritySectionNumber ports
  Number(string) (empty/whitespace → 0; full numeric parse else NaN) and String(number)
  (whole drops the fraction; fractional keeps minimal decimal). SecuritySectionSignalValue
  models the backend `string | boolean | null` union (a `number` case for numeric
  percentages) with numericReading (`Number(true)=1`/`Number(false)=0`/`Number(str)`) and
  stringValue (`String(true)="true"`/etc.). All unit tested directly.

  Accent fidelity (ADR-006 semantic, not literal): the web MetricCard `color` prop tints
  ONLY the icon chip (bg/ring/glyph), not the value. green → statusSuccess, cyan →
  statusInfo; the locked/sentry/doors/windows tiles flip green↔cyan by state. The value
  reads textPrimary; the label reads textSecondary.

  Two-prop modelling: the web empty branch keys ONLY on `securityData` (`securityData ?
  grid : EmptyState`); the always-present `state` flags (is_locked / sentry_mode) are
  surfaced only inside the grid. Modelled as SecuritySectionReading carrying both the
  VehicleState flags and the SecurityEvent door/window signals; a nil reading is the web
  `!securityData` empty branch (so the state-derived tiles render iff a security reading
  exists — web parity, unit tested).

  Seams (P1/S8): SecuritySectionSource (one coalesced snapshot: reading + loading/error +
    connectivity) → SecuritySectionModel (@Observable). Previews/tests inject
    InMemorySecuritySectionSource; the view performs no networking.
    Telemetry (P1/S11): view.opened with surface slug "SecuritySection", emitted once.
    i18n (P1/S10): every string via SecuritySectionStrings; 0 hardcoded English literals in
    native code. The "{{count}}" token is substituted by SecuritySectionStrings.windowsOpen
    (i18next-style, also tolerating single-brace {count}). The raw door_state string is
    device/data text carried through unchanged, not a translated string.

